Deployed as static files, not a Jekyll site.

GitHub Pages runs Jekyll over the published tree unless this file exists, and Jekyll
drops anything whose name starts with an underscore. Nothing Vite emits starts with one
today, so this is insurance rather than a fix for a live bug - but the failure it guards
against is a silent 404 on one asset, which is exactly the shape of bug that costs an
afternoon.

The Actions deployment used by .github/workflows/pages.yml publishes the artifact as-is
and never invokes Jekyll, so this only matters if the repo is ever switched to the older
"deploy from a branch" setting.
